# Findings accepted on purpose. Each one has its reasoning in
# docs/security/accepted-risks.md and an expiry date: when it passes, Trivy
# reports the finding again and it has to be looked at anew. Never add an ID
# here without the matching entry in that document.

# postgres:16.15-alpine — gosu 1.19 is built with Go 1.24.6. gosu runs once,
# as root, to drop to the postgres user and exec the server; it opens no
# socket and parses no certificate, archive or HTTP message, which is where
# these standard-library flaws live. Upstream: github.com/tianon/gosu, "CVEs".
